From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:11:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] TCSocket: encode and decode STCPacket field by field

Send() and receive() copied the memory of the struct to and from the
socket. That ties the wire format to the compiler, ABI and byte order,
puts whatever is in the two padding bytes on the wire, and accepts any
byte as the is_last bool or as codec_in. A bool that is not 0 or 1 is
undefined behaviour in C++.

Add EncodeTCPacket()/DecodeTCPacket() in TCPacketCodec.{h,cpp}. They
write each field at a fixed offset with a fixed width in little-endian
order, write the padding as zero and ignore it on read. The output is
byte for byte the struct memory on x86-64 and arm64 Linux, so a peer
without this change still works. Decode refuses an is_last that is not
0 or 1 and a codec_in that is not a defined codec (for a ping only
codec_in is checked). A refused packet closes the link; the reconnect
starts again on a packet boundary.
